  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A rational function is a ratio of polynomials. The new feature is the <strong>asymptote</strong> — a line the graph approaches but never meets — produced by values that make the denominator zero.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Definition 4.1 — Asymptotes",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>For \\( y=\\dfrac{1}{x-h}+k \\): a <strong>vertical asymptote</strong> at \\( x=h \\) (denominator zero) and a <strong>horizontal asymptote</strong> at \\( y=k \\) (the end-behaviour value).</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Slide the asymptotes around. The two amber dashed lines are \\( x=h \\) and \\( y=k \\); the curve hugs them in every corner.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "canvasId": "ratCanvas",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Rational function &amp; asymptotes",
          "ar": null
        },
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A rational function with movable vertical and horizontal asymptotes",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "ratDataBtn",
          "panelId": "ratDataPanel",
          "descId": "ratDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "ratDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Sampled points on each branch of the curve",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "ratH",
            "label": {
              "en": "Vertical shift of asymptote &nbsp; <b>h</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -4,
            "max": 4,
            "value": 1,
            "step": 1,
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Vertical shift of asymptote h",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "ratK",
            "label": {
              "en": "Horizontal asymptote &nbsp; <b>k</b>",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": -3,
            "max": 3,
            "value": 0,
            "step": 1,
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Horizontal asymptote k",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "ratVA",
            "label": {
              "en": "vertical asymptote",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          },
          {
            "id": "ratHA",
            "label": {
              "en": "horizontal asymptote",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": "—",
            "colorClass": "amber"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "<b id=\"ratEq\" class=\"mono\">y = 1 / (x − 1)</b>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Simplify \\( \\dfrac{x^{2}-9}{x-3} \\).</p><p>Factor and cancel (for \\( x\\neq 3 \\)):</p>\\[ \\frac{(x-3)(x+3)}{x-3}=x+3. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 4.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( \\dfrac{1}{x}+\\dfrac{1}{2}=1 \\).</p><p>Then \\( \\dfrac{1}{x}=\\dfrac12 \\), so:</p>\\[ x=2. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Rational expressions and equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>A rational expression is a ratio of polynomials. Simplify by factoring and cancelling common factors. Multiply LCD to solve rational equations; check for extraneous solutions.</p>",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Simplify",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Factor numerator and denominator; cancel common factors",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Add/subtract",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Find LCD; rewrite each fraction; combine numerators",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Multiply",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Multiply numerators and denominators; simplify",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Solve equation",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Multiply both sides by LCD; solve; check for excluded values",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Simplify \\( \\dfrac{x^2-4}{x^2-x-2} \\).</p>\\[ \\frac{(x-2)(x+2)}{(x-2)(x+1)}=\\frac{x+2}{x+1},\\quad x\\neq 2,-1. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Sketch \\(y=\\dfrac{2x+1}{x-3}\\), showing all asymptotes and intercepts.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Vertical asymptote: \\(x=3\\). Horizontal asymptote: \\(y=2\\) (leading coefficients). \\(y\\)-intercept: \\(y=-1/3\\). \\(x\\)-intercept: \\(x=-1/2\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
